/DA (\057Helv 9\0565 Tf 0\056066667 0\056066667 0\056066667 rg)
/DV (THE PROBLEM\012Small business owners make financial decisions with information scattered across bank statements\054 invoices\054 email\054\012chat and employee folders\056 Missing documents\054 unexplained spending and seasonal cash shortages create manual\012work and late surprises\056 Owners need someone to follow up with the team and explain what requires their attention\056\012\012YOUR SOLUTION\012Scout is an autonomous AI CFO that connects financial records with the context behind them\056 It investigates missing\012invoices\054 checks costs against business activity\054 forecasts liquidity and proposes next steps\056 Instead of stopping at an\012alert\054 it follows the issue through to a documented outcome\056 Routine work is automated\073 consequential decisions\012require human approval\056\012\012THE WORKING PROTOTYPE\012In the Pizzeria Amalfi demo\054 users inspect transactions\054 invoices\054 agent tasks\054 evidence and an audit log\056 Scout\012searches authorized company sources for missing documents\054 reconciles amounts and requests help through Slack\012when needed\056 Owners can approve or reject actions\054 ask questions in chat and explore cash\055flow forecasts and\012what\055if spending scenarios\056 A separate Strategy loop produces cited news briefings using optional hosted research\012providers\056 Banking uses demo data or a sandbox\073 financial execution is simulated\056\012\012BEHIND THE BUILD\012Python\054 FastAPI\054 LangGraph and PostgreSQL connect durable jobs\054 tools and approval checkpoints to a Next\056js\012dashboard\056 MCP exposes company records\054 HR and authorized workstation files\056 IBM Granite runs through vLLM on\012Red Hat OpenShift AI\073 NeMo Guardrails screens prompts\054 documents and responses\056 XGBoost computes forecasts\054\012with Jupyter\054 Optuna and MLflow supporting training\054 tuning\054 tracing and evaluation\056 We built the reconciliation\012workflows\054 policy engine\054 task and approval experience\054 connectors and dashboard around these existing tools\056\012Financial calculations and policy checks stay in code\073 the LLM interprets context and explains results\056\012\012CHALLENGES AND DISCOVERIES\012Connecting a small self\055hosted model to reliable tools required explicit tool\055calling configuration and fallback parsing\056\012Persistent jobs and approval state were essential when work paused for a person\056 We also found that a seasonal\012cash decline is not automatically a cash shortage\072 recommendations must use the actual balance and safety buffer\056\012External documents need screening before entering model context\054 and connector setup must distinguish configured\012access from verified access\056\012\012RESULTS AND NEXT STEPS\012We connected investigation\054 explained recommendations and owner responses in one auditable prototype\056 Recorded\012cluster smoke checks passed all 11 checks\054 including Granite tool calls\054 MCP reads and database access\056 Local\012verification covered policy\054 persistence\054 tenant isolation\054 approvals and responsive light\057dark layouts\056 Validation uses\012organizer and synthetic demo data\054 with no measured customer savings yet\056 Next steps are broader live\055provider\012validation\054 more representative forecast backtesting and production hardening before real financial execution\056)
/F 4
/FT /Tx
/Ff 4096
