l experience\054 connectors and dashboard around these existing tools\056\012Financial calculations and policy checks stay in code\073 the LLM interprets context and explains results\056\012\012CHALLENGES AND DISCOVERIES\012Connecting a small self\055hosted model to reliable tools required explicit tool\055calling configuration and fallback parsing\056\012Persistent jobs and approval state were essential when work paused for a person\056 We also found that a seasonal\012cash decline is not automatically a cash shortage\072 recommendations must use the actual balance and safety buffer\056\012External documents need screening before entering model context\054 and connector setup must distinguish configured\012access from verified access\056\012\012RESULTS AND NEXT STEPS\012We connected investigation\054 explained recommendations and owner responses in one auditable prototype\056 Recorded\012cluster smoke checks passed all 11 checks\054 including Granite tool calls\054 MCP reads and database access\056 Local\012verification covered policy\054 persistence\054 tenant isolation\054 approvals and responsive light\057dark layouts\056 Validation uses\012organizer and synthetic demo data\054 with no measured customer savings yet\056 Next steps are broader live\055provider\012validation\054 more representative forecast backtesting and production hardening before real financial execution\056)
